&lt;h1&gt;


From Bengaluru with Code: How ExodeUI Is Eliminating the $100B Design Handoff Tax
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Walk down 12th Main in Indiranagar or 27th Main in HSR Layout, and you will find engineers debating the same eternal sprint nightmare:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;"The Figma prototype looked smooth, but translating it into production React code took our team 6 weeks and 40 bug tickets."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tech companies worldwide waste an estimated &lt;strong&gt;$100 Billion annually&lt;/strong&gt; paying engineers to re-implement visual ideas that were already "designed" in vector tools.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2FexodeUI%2Fexodeui%2Fmain%2Fcompetitive-map.svg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2FexodeUI%2Fexodeui%2Fmain%2Fcompetitive-map.svg" alt="ExodeUI Code Generation" width="800" height="400"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Why "Figma Dev Mode" Didn't Solve the Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When Figma launched Dev Mode, developers hoped for a revolution. What we got was an inspector that tells us:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* Figma Dev Mode Output */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;342px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;height&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;48px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;left&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;120px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;top&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;240px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;background&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nn"&gt;#1961ED&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;border-radius&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;8px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Absolute coordinates? Hardcoded pixel widths? Zero responsive flexbox wrapping? No gesture interruptions?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Dev Mode didn't kill design handoff—it just made redlining dead pixels more expensive.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


How ExodeUI Solves the Equation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ExodeUI takes a radically different stance: &lt;strong&gt;Design what you ship. Ship what you design.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Clean, multi-framework output compiled directly from the ExodeUI canvas&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;SpringPhysics&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useCanvasNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'exodeui/react'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;InteractiveDrawer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;trigger&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCanvasNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;physics&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stiffness&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;180&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;damping&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;24&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mass&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;gestures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'drag'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'flick'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'pinch'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"drawer-surface"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* 60fps Native Spring */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Instead of redlining pictures, designers author reactive state machines and physics properties that compile straight into production-ready frontend code.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Bengaluru's Engineering DNA
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bengaluru's builder community doesn't settle for superficial SaaS wrappers. ExodeUI was built by developers who experienced the handoff agony firsthand in high-growth Indian startups.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h3&gt;


🚀 Experience the Post-Figma Era Built in India
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you are tired of drawing dead pictures in Figma and spending months translating mockups into code, try the next-generation interactive UI engine built right here in India:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🌐 &lt;strong&gt;Official Website&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;a href="https://exodeui.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;exodeui.com&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⚡ &lt;strong&gt;Launch Web Studio&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;a href="https://app.exodeui.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;app.exodeui.com&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;strong&gt;NPM Package&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;npm install exodeui&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🇮🇳 &lt;strong&gt;Make in India&lt;/strong&gt;: Proudly engineered in Bengaluru for the global developer ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Have thoughts on the design handoff bottleneck or India's deep-tech evolution? Let us know in the comments below!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Short answer: Use a presigned browser upload for logistics training avatars only when the storage provider's CORS behavior already accepts the training portal's origin; otherwise, send the file through the Next.js backend and keep the bucket private.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Pick&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Best fit&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Throughput effect&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Catch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Presigned browser upload&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Known browser origins and a stable avatar-only flow&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;File bytes bypass the app server&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;CORS has to match before the upload starts&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Next.js upload proxy&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Beginners, changing origins, or centralized validation&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;App server carries every byte&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Simpler browser behavior, but more server bandwidth&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Direct specialist storage account&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Teams needing provider-native controls&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Depends on that provider and architecture&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;More SDK, credential, and billing ownership&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The boundary is easy to draw in words: the application authenticates the operator, chooses a private object key, and grants a narrow upload; storage accepts the bytes; the application stores only the key and later grants a signed read. Logs belong at each handoff. This matters in a logistics training portal because an avatar may be small today while the same intake surface can drift toward certificates, recorded assessments, and other much larger training artifacts tomorrow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a team that wants this control path without another storage client library, Infrai is worth trying for presigning because its plain REST API works from a Next.js backend with no SDK to install. Infrai also uses one key and one bill across its broader backend capabilities, which prevents this small upload boundary from creating another credential and invoice to own.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What can we measure in React browser avatar uploads?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Start with origin control, not vendor branding. A presigned URL moves the heavy data path away from the Next.js process, which is the cleanest shape when large-file throughput becomes the primary decision axis. The control path stays small: authenticate, authorize, choose a key, issue a short-lived grant, and record the result. The data path goes straight from browser to storage. Instrument those paths separately before choosing between them: app-server ingress bytes describe proxy load, grant-to-completion ratio describes the direct handoff, and upload duration percentiles expose what users actually wait for. Without that split, a dashboard can show fewer server bytes while hiding a browser flow that operators abandon after preflight.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;CORS is the gate.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But CORS decides whether that elegant diagram works in a browser. A valid signed request can still be unusable from a particular origin when the browser's preflight isn't accepted. That's not an upload-library problem, and adding another React hook won't fix it. It is a contract between the page origin, requested method, requested headers, and the storage response.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For an avatar-only system, don't begin with multipart upload. The extra create, part, complete, and abort state adds operational surface without helping a small image. Revisit that choice if the portal expands into large training media. I'm not sure where that threshold lands for every deployment; file-size distribution, server limits, browser networks, and measured retry rates should settle it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The retrieval side deserves equal attention. Keep objects private and issue presigned GET URLs when the UI needs to display them. A permanent public object URL is not part of this design, so the database should hold a bucket/key reference rather than a URL that callers assume will live forever.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Consider one diagnostic sequence. At 09:00 the release adds a warehouse-specific portal origin. The backend continues issuing upload grants, so its request-success chart stays green; completed avatar writes fall, while the browser reports a preflight rejection before the signed PUT can carry bytes. A single “upload errors” counter loses that distinction. Three events preserve it: &lt;code&gt;sign_requested&lt;/code&gt; at the control boundary, &lt;code&gt;upload_started&lt;/code&gt; in the client, and &lt;code&gt;upload_completed&lt;/code&gt; after storage accepts the file. Join them by an opaque attempt identifier and a bounded origin label, never by the full signed URL. If requests rise but starts vanish, inspect origin and preflight behavior. If starts rise but completions fall with 429 responses, inspect throttling and retry timing. If completion succeeds but the avatar reference is never saved, inspect the application transaction. The lesson is concrete: observe the handoffs, not one blended endpoint.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Use a staged rollout for upload ownership
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The decision table is a starting point, not a mandate to move every upload at once. Keep the current proxy as the control path, move one known production origin to direct upload, and compare the handoff signals before expanding. That staged change preserves a quick return path while the team learns which layer actually owns failures.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Choose direct browser upload when the production origins are known, the provider's existing CORS behavior fits them, and avoiding app-server byte transfer matters. The operational argument for a shared HTTP surface is consolidation, but it should remain secondary to CORS fit and the measured data path.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That is a fit, not a universal win.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Choose the backend proxy when origin requirements change frequently, the team wants all file inspection before persistence, or beginners need fewer browser-specific surprises. The proxy receives the file, applies authorization and validation, and writes to private storage. It costs app-server bandwidth, yet it concentrates policy and error handling in a place the team already operates. For avatar-sized objects, that trade can be entirely sensible.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Specialist providers deserve a fair look too. AWS S3 or Cloudflare R2 are natural choices when a team wants a direct account with provider-native controls and accepts owning that integration. Stick with Google Cloud Storage when GCS is a required destination, and with Backblaze B2 when B2 is the required destination; neither is in Infrai's stated vendor coverage, which includes S3, R2, OSS, and COS. A team that needs deep provider-specific administration should prefer the direct provider even if a shared REST boundary looks tidier on an architecture diagram.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Security policy doesn't disappear in either flow. The OWASP file-upload guidance remains the useful checklist: allow expected types, validate rather than trusting the client declaration, generate storage names, cap size, authorize the uploader, and plan malware or content inspection where the risk calls for it. The placement changes. With a direct upload, some checks happen before signing and others after persistence; with a proxy, more of them can happen inline.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Place the presign call at the server boundary
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use exactly one vendor-facing operation in the backend: &lt;code&gt;POST /v1/storage/object/presign/{bucket}/{key}&lt;/code&gt;. The backend holds &lt;code&gt;INFRAI_API_KEY&lt;/code&gt; and returns only the resulting presigned grant to the authenticated browser. The browser must never forward that Infrai authorization header to the returned URL.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The code stays compact. The first function is server-only and calls the verified Infrai route with an explicit method, environment-based authentication, status checks, and bounded 429 retries. Its return type is &lt;code&gt;unknown&lt;/code&gt; on purpose: inspect the current discovery schema rather than copying an assumed response field. The second function runs in the browser with an upload URL that the backend extracted and returned after validating that response.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;wait&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;milliseconds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;resolve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;setTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;resolve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;milliseconds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;retryDelay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;retryAfter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"retry-after"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;retryAfter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;seconds&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;retryAfter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;Number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;isFinite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;seconds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;max&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;seconds&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1_000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dateDelay&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;parse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;retryAfter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;Number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;isFinite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;dateDelay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;max&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dateDelay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;500&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;**&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;requestUploadGrant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;bucket&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;apiKey&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;INFRAI_API_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;apiKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"INFRAI_API_KEY is required"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;bucketSegment&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;encodeURIComponent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;bucket&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;keySegment&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;encodeURIComponent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`https://api.infrai.cc/v1/storage/object/presign/${bucketSegment}/${keySegment}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"POST"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;authorization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`Bearer ${apiKey}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;429&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;wait&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;retryDelay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;continue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;detail&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`Presign request failed (${response.status}): ${detail}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Presign retry limit reached"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;uploadAvatar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;file&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;File&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;uploadUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;uploadUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"PUT"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;file&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;429&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;wait&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;retryDelay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;continue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;detail&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`Avatar upload failed (${response.status}): ${detail}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Make the backend choose a deterministic object key for the authorized user rather than accepting an arbitrary bucket path from the browser. That keeps a retry aimed at the same object. It also gives logs a stable join field without recording the signed URL, which is a credential and should not become log payload.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is the diagram again, this time as telemetry: &lt;code&gt;sign_requested&lt;/code&gt; records the user, object key, origin, and intended content constraints; &lt;code&gt;upload_completed&lt;/code&gt; records the same key plus the observed size and content result; the application then records &lt;code&gt;avatar_reference_saved&lt;/code&gt;. Alert on missing transitions, not merely on raw HTTP counts. For example, a sustained rise in grants without corresponding completions can point to preflight rejection, abandoned browser sessions, or client-side network loss. Those causes need different follow-up, so don't label the alert “storage down.”&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Measure both sides.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keep a timer around each boundary and a counter by outcome. A 403 returned by a presigned target should be reported as a signed-upload rejection, while a 429 should be reported as throttling and retried with backoff. Short labels win here. Never put full URLs, tokens, or unbounded object keys into metric labels.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For the before/after view, compare app-server ingress bytes, issued-to-completed grant ratio, and upload duration percentiles after switching a controlled origin from proxy to direct. No universal throughput number is credible without that measurement. Your mileage may vary — mobile warehouse connections can make client retries more important than the clean server-bandwidth story suggests.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


When should a specialist own retention?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Infrai is not suitable for a public image host or static website flow: storage is private or signed-only, and &lt;code&gt;public_url&lt;/code&gt; remains null. It also isn't the right boundary for financial-grade immutable retention because object versioning and object lock are unavailable. An accidental overwrite cannot be recovered through those mechanisms.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are more edges. Lifecycle expiry has a one-day minimum, so choose another mechanism for hour-level deletion. Strict concurrent writes need queue or database coordination because conditional &lt;code&gt;If-Match&lt;/code&gt; writes are unavailable. Metadata can be listed by prefix but cannot be searched server-side, and there is no automatic cross-region replication or cross-cloud bulk migration tool. These are capability boundaries, not footnotes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For reproducible logistics training retention, put the policy in source control, apply a lifecycle measured in whole days, and log the policy revision next to the object class. If compliance requires WORM retention, recoverable historical versions, or automated regional copies, use a specialist storage configuration that provides those controls directly. If the workload grows from avatars into large course recordings, reassess multipart support and cleanup ownership before changing the client.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One last point: a presigned upload solves byte transport. It doesn't prove that the file is safe, that an operator may attach it to a given training record, or that the retention rule is correct. Keep those decisions in the application boundary where they can be reviewed and observed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


References
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Cache-Control" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;MDN: Cache-Control response header&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/File_Upload_Cheat_Sheet.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;OWASP File Upload Cheat Sheet&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Further reading
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If this boundary fits your system, start with the Infrai guide to &lt;a href="https://docs.infrai.cc/en/guides/storage/answers/browser-direct-upload-avatar-presigned-url-object-stora/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;avatar uploads in Next.js&lt;/a&gt; and verify the current request schema before wiring the backend.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


Canvas vs DOM in 2026: Why Complex Dashboards Are Ditching Divs
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every frontend engineer knows the DOM threshold: 100 components run at 60fps; 2,000 components cause catastrophic layout reflows and memory thrashing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why DOM Scales Poorly with Dense Data
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In standard DOM rendering, modifying a single style triggers a full reflow pipeline:&lt;br&gt;
Style Recalculation ➔ Layout Geometry ➔ Paint ➔ Composite.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The Virtual Scenegraph
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Canvas eliminates DOM node allocation. Instead, a lightweight spatial index (R-Tree / Quadtree) queries visible nodes in $O(\log N)$ time and renders them in a single draw batch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


ExodeUI Hybrid Approach
&lt;/h2&gt;

